+**Memory Complexity**: $O(1)$ for primitives. Scene graph size depends on the number of primitives [G].
+**Measured Performance**: Highly efficient on GPUs due to lack of branching and simple arithmetic [G].
 **Strengths**:
-- Infinite resolution (analytic).
-- Easy to implement and debug.
-- Compact memory footprint.
+- Infinite resolution (analytic) [G].
+- Easy to implement and debug [G].
+- Compact memory footprint [G].
 - Natural support for smooth blending and morphing [S3, unofficial].
 **Limitations**:
-- Cannot represent arbitrary topology (e.g., self-intersections in complex ways without CSG).
-- Normals are approximate if computed via finite differences.
-- Hard to represent highly detailed organic geometry without noise primitives or texture mapping [S6, unofficial].
-**When to use**: Ideal for real-time rendering of stylized, geometric, or procedural scenes.
-**When not to use**: When photorealistic detail from scanned meshes is required, or when the geometry is too complex for efficient CSG evaluation.
